  "term": "MSI",
  "definition": "MSI, in this source, refers to the Goldsmiths Musical Sophistication Index, a self-report assessment used to measure musical sophistication in adolescence and adulthood. It is presented as an instrument for studying engagement-related aspects of musicality, in contrast to a child-adapted version developed for younger ages.",
